{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1520317-converting-cryokinesis-to-a-vampire-v20-discipline","id":1520317,"title":"Converting Cryokinesis to a Vampire v20 discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-10T12:05:02-07:00","id":1520317,"title":"Converting Cryokinesis to a Vampire v20 discipline","content":"Greetings everyone,<br /> <br /> as the title suggests, i am trying to homebrew a new discipline for a Pander character that has a general ice theme going (chill wind, frozen touch, obtenebration, snuffing out flames with his presence, feeding restriction to frozen blood and Tzimisce Clan Flaw to have to rest in ice or snow - freezer)<br /> <br /> Since Pander can create their own disciplines (Guide to Pariahs and Outcasts) the easiest things seems to be taking something that already exists and adapting it. Cryokinesis fits the character perfectly so i wanted to adapt that.<br /> <br /> So first issue is the rolls. Cryokinesis uses &quot;Psi Score&quot; as basis which if i understand correctly, goes from 1-10. The only Vampire thing that could work here is Willpower, also seems to make sense.<br /> or substitute for an attribute and an abaility roll like koldunism does like way of earth, stamina+occult?<br /> <br /> Second issue is the actual rolls for successes, would that also be plain willpower or stamina+occult? (Stamina seems to make sense for me cause you leech heat energy from surrounding so mus withstand the heat yourself and occult is about the only skill that seems fitting, except maybe survival)<br /> <br /> Third issue is ressource - Bloodpoints seem to substitute nicely for Psi points, but afaik there is no limit on Psipoints per turn, so Cryofreeze needs 3 BP and i was wondering it it was more sensoble to use 1 BP and 1 WP instead so you dont have to charge up 3 turns.<br /> <br /> These out of the way, the actual powers...<br /> <br /> 1. Thermal screen seems absolutely useless to vampires as they take halfed bashing damage and there is almost no powers in the game (except koldunism way of wind 2) that actually deal cold damage So id extend that to become an iceshield that adds soak to any bashing or lethal source?<br /> <br /> 2. Hypothermic blast seems alright as is<br /> <br /> 3. Flash Freeze seems right as is BUT id switch it with 1. Thermal Screen cause extra soak seems way more usefull than freezing liquids unless one allows to freeze vitae inside vampires effectively removing Blood points from their pool temporarily (like net successes in a resisted roll vs stamina and survival)<br /> <br /> 4. Heat sink could become real good if it allows to fight off fire damage including incendiary ammo or flamethrowers<br /> <br /> 5. Cryofreeze seems good but id change that its either unsoakable in general (not just no armor bonus) or change the damage from lethal to Aggravated (loosing limbs does agg and this can freeze of limbs) Otherwise its weaker than Hypothermic blast and a level 5 power kinda should be awesome<br /> <br /> In General i think tis not inbalanced given that say Koldunism and Thaumaturgy actually give you more flexibility, better shields and more agg damage (like lure of flames) and cryokinesis doesnt trigger R\u00f6tschreck tests.<br /> <br /> So im open for your ideas and glad to hear some =)<br /> <br /> Btw what was the exact roll to roll cryokinesis?\u200b Just Psi Score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-10-2023, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov